@startuml login-session-logout
title User Service - Login, session validation and logout
autonumber
hide footbox

participant Browser
participant "Other Service" as Other
participant "User Service" as User
database PostgreSQL as DB

note over Other, User
  Other Service illustrates the intended integration contract.
  Its application behaviour is not implemented by User Service.
end note

== Login ==
Browser -> User: POST /api/v1/auth/login\nemail + password
User -> DB: Begin transaction; load and lock verified account
DB --> User: Account and password hash (if found)
User -> User: Check password

alt Valid credentials
  User -> User: Generate random session token
  User -> DB: Store token digest, user ID and expiry\nReplace this browser's prior session, if present
  User -> DB: Commit
  DB --> User: Committed
  User --> Browser: 200 + HttpOnly session cookie
else Invalid credentials or unverified account
  User -> DB: Roll back
  User --> Browser: 401 - login rejected
end

== Protected request after successful login ==
Browser -> Other: Protected request + session cookie
Other -> User: POST /internal/v1/sessions/validate\nsessionToken + service credential
User -> User: Check service credential

alt Service credential invalid
  User --> Other: 401 - invalid service credentials
  Other --> Browser: Reject request
else Service credential valid
  User -> DB: Find unexpired session by token digest\nand read current user roles
  alt Session valid
    DB --> User: User ID, roles and session expiry
    User --> Other: 200 - userId, roles, expiresAt
    Other -> Other: Check permission for the operation
    Other --> Browser: Result, or 403 if forbidden
  else Session expired or revoked
    DB --> User: No valid session
    User --> Other: 401 - invalid session
    Other --> Browser: 401 - please log in
  else Database unavailable
    DB --> User: Lookup fails
    User --> Other: 503 - authentication unavailable
    Other --> Browser: 503 - try again later
  end
end

note over Other, User
  Validate once per protected incoming request; do not cache success
  across requests initially. On timeout/network failure, fail closed.
  Other services enforce their own permissions and never read User DB.
end note

== Logout ==
Browser -> User: POST /api/v1/auth/logout\nsession cookie
User -> DB: Delete current session
DB --> User: Deleted
User --> Browser: 204 + clear cookie
note over Browser, User
  Subsequent validation of that session fails.
  A request authorised before logout may still finish.
end note
@enduml
